-- title:
--   The periodic repetition of a smooth collared template is smooth
-- statement:
--   A velocity $v$ has time collars when $v(t,\cdot)=0$ for $t<\frac14$ and for $t>\frac34$. Its repetition is the $1$-periodic field $\tilde v(t,x)=\sum_{n\in\mathbb Z}v(t-n,x)$. If $v$ is jointly smooth and has time collars, then
--   $$
--   (t,x)\mapsto\tilde v(t,x)\ \text{ is }C^\infty\text{ on }\mathbb R\times\mathbb R^3 .
--   $$
--
--   This gives smoothness of the eventually periodic velocity built from one period of motion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/Periodic.lean#L46-L61

